Formally, an adaptive hybrid representation is a set of up to a fixed number of features, the budget, selected from several base representations of the same molecules. A search chooses it for one dataset and one downstream model, so a different dataset, split or model gives a different hybrid. The hybrid is an input rather than a model, so any standard supervised model can be trained on it. It is intended for base representations that describe different aspects of the molecule, such as PDV descriptors, ECFP4 bits, graph embeddings and sequence embeddings.

