We score features using LightGBM gain importance, SHapley Additive exPlanations (SHAP) values for tree ensembles (TreeSHAP) and DeepLIFT (Deep Learning Important FeaTures) \citep{Shrikumar2017}. LightGBM gain measures how much a feature reduced the training loss where trees split on it \citep{ke2017lightgbm}. TreeSHAP gives each feature's exact Shapley value for each molecule's prediction from a tree model \citep{Lundberg2020}. DeepLIFT measures how much a feature moves the output of a small network, trained with Adam \citep{Kingma2015}, away from its output on an all-zero reference input, which after standardization places every feature at its training mean \citep{Shrikumar2017, Kokhlikyan2020, Ancona2018}. On Caco-2, the median share of features scoring above 0 was 30\% for LightGBM gain, 70\% for TreeSHAP and 90\% for DeepLIFT (preliminary, over 10 representations and 3 folds). Table~\ref{tab:importance_methods} gives the settings of each method, including the pre-screen of representations wider than 2,000 features.

