Methods that handle noisy labels by comparing each label with its neighbors or with held-out predictions, such as nearest-neighbor editing \citep{Wilson1972}, filtering by classifiers trained on other folds \citep{Brodley1999} and confident learning \citep{Northcutt2021}, each depend on the feature space in which they work. We ask three research questions, each answered in one results section:
