Four further methods are tested on the recorded labels with nothing injected. C-Mixup, a form of mixup \citep{Zhang2018mixup}, adds one training molecule for each existing one by mixing its features and label with those of a partner that has a similar label. Target-noise bagging averages several models, each fitted on the labels plus fresh random noise. Pair down-weighting takes the closest 1\% of training pairs and gives weight 0.25 to both molecules of any pair whose labels differ by more than $3\sqrt{2}\,\hat\sigma$, where $\hat\sigma$ is the noise standard deviation estimated from the label differences of close pairs. Down-weighting suspect molecules lowers the weight of training molecules with a high noise score (Table~\ref{tab:noise_estimators}), over 11 settings of the score and the strength.

