A method tuned closely to one dataset loses generality. The tasks in this thesis span binding affinity, ADME, quantum-chemical properties and antibodies, and this range is the reason learned models are used at all. Simple methods do not generalize automatically either: feature selection needs tuning for each dataset, which is why the search sweeps its settings, and the search itself can overfit (Discussion, Chapter~\ref{chap:method}). The balance is to fix the simple, robust parts, such as a tree ensemble or nearest neighbors on a small feature set, and search only what varies by dataset.



